  "description": "MUZGIA crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C70 H68 Cl4 Co2 Dy4 N10 O32,2(C2 H6 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Dy1B (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy2B (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Co1B (Co) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.191-3.926 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.68-110.85°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C74H80Cl4Co2Dy4N10O34. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
